  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Emergency Lifesaving Assistances on WASH and Shelter/NFI in Rakhine (Mocha Cyclone Response)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtCDN-ZOA will work with local partners, site leaders and volunteers to provide WASH and Shelter/NFI support to IDP sites in Sittwe and Kyauktaw affected by cyclone Mocha. This work will complement planned work WASH and Shelter/NFI work under MM-22/DDA-3415/SA1?WASH-SNFI-P-N/INGO/24105 which CDN-ZOA works in consortium with PIN and local implementing partners. In addition, the funds will be supplemented by in-kind supports available for the response through UNOPS and UNHCR in these areas. Support will focus on the provision of cash transfers,&#xa0;distribution of shelter/NFI items and WASH rehabilitation activities.lt/pgtltpgtThe humanitarian situation in Myanmar has significantly deteriorated in the aftermath of cyclone Mocha. Initial field visits and rapid needs assessments across WASH and Shelter clusters are showing significant to total distruction of shelters, communal building and services&#xa0;and WASH facilities in sites across Sittwe and Kyauktaw. Urgent needs identified include&#xa0;shelter, clean water and food assistance,&#xa0;with repairs for WASH facilities (latrines, bathhouses, water storage, etc)&#xa0;as well as support to access clean water.&#xa0;There are also significant concerns about shortages of drinking water and the risk of waterborne disease.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
